# ============================================================================
# Cloud Functions environment configuration
# ============================================================================
#
# There is INTENTIONALLY nothing to fill in here today.
#
# Cloud Functions (unlike server/, a standalone Express process — see
# server/.env.example) run inside Firebase's own infrastructure and receive
# their Firebase Admin project credentials automatically. There is no
# service account JSON or GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS to configure for
# functions/ in either the emulator or in production deploys.
#
# If a future function needs a third-party secret (e.g. an SMS/email
# provider API key), set it with the Firebase CLI's `functions:secrets:set`
# (Secret Manager-backed) rather than a plain .env file, and document the
# secret name here. As of this initial build, no function needs one.
